# PLAYWRIGHT CONCEPT: Environment Configuration
# What it is: .env provides runtime values like usernames, passwords, and API base URLs without hard-coding them.
# Why Playwright does it this way: tests should be portable across environments and secrets can be kept out of source control.
# If you're coming from Selenium/RestAssured: this is similar to properties files or environment variables, but Playwright reads them naturally in config and tests.
# Common mistake to avoid: committing credentials or using different values across browsers without a clear source-of-truth.

SAUCEDEMO_USERNAME=standard_user
SAUCEDEMO_PASSWORD=secret_sauce
REQRES_BASE_URL=https://reqres.in/api
